# Normalize line endings to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# The reproducibility exporter embeds *verbatim* recipe bytes -- environment.yaml,
# load.py, extended_metadata.yaml -- into each corpus flowsheet (content + a
# sha256 of those bytes). If a Windows checkout materializes those recipes as
# CRLF (git's core.autocrlf default), a re-export would bake CRLF content and a
# CRLF-based sha256 into the corpus, making the reproducibility block mismatch
# the LF-committed recipes and differ from a Linux/CI checkout. Pinning eol=lf
# keeps exports portable and byte-stable regardless of the exporting machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never munge binary assets.
*.png binary
